{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c19-closing.txt'","aggregated_output":"Before you return the answer, check it once. Read each evidence item back as the analyst following the company and keep it when you would write it in this week's notes because it makes some question's answer more or less likely, about the company or its customers, suppliers, competitors, regulators or the economy. Ask first whether it is new: repeated common knowledge, a long-standing situation retold and an unargued view are noise. Do not drop a reported step, figure, guidance, forecast or decision because the item retells it or another outlet reported it before: a later step compares each statement with the evidence already stored and records a repeat there. Guidance, a forecast, a plan or a decision still in force keeps its place even when retold, including a change to a plan, design or schedule that another outlet reported days or weeks before. Judge the action or information itself, not its verb tense, and do not take a statement as old because its date is missing. Fitting one of the four kinds does not keep an item. A missing amount, date or scale never drops an item on its own: a forecast, a rumour, a counter-example or a distant or conditional statement is judged like any other.\nThese are not kept, even when a named party states them. What a row says it does not cover goes back to the test above, unless the row says it is kept:\n- background the analyst already knew, such as the company's history (\"the company was founded in 1998\"); an arrangement the item only describes as in place, even when no date is given: customers or partners that use, host, run or have built on the company's products, and the benefits they describe from that use (\"two airlines fly the planemaker's jets\"; \"three insurers run claims on the company's software and report faster payouts\"); a partnership, contract, plant or investment the item itself dates to an earlier month or year with no new step (\"earlier this year the company partnered with the glassmaker on three plants\"; \"in May it signed a $3 billion cloud contract\"); it does not cover a step the item reports as news, taken, decided, planned or under way (an order, a selection, an integration, an expansion, a deployment), even when it gives no date (\"the retailer's largest supplier is opening its own stores, people familiar said this week\"; \"the two largest cement makers are adding kilns to meet demand\"), nor a customer's, supplier's or partner's newly disclosed revenue, capacity, orders or contracted amount; a deal the item mentions as already existing is an arrangement in place even with its amount (\"a rival airline already leases 40 of the same jets\");\n- a typical claim that is common knowledge, without a figure and a specific account: that a firm leads or competes, that demand is strong or supply tight, a general risk (\"if demand slows it would hurt\"); a number does not lift a familiar position (\"the rival grocer has led this market for years and still holds 40%\"); it does not cover a dated forecast of a shortage, a price or demand (\"the steelmaker expects the shortage to peak next year and last until 2028\"), a competitor's newly reported share, volume or price in the company's market (\"the local rival now holds about half of the regional market, worth about $5 billion\"), nor a reported movement of a named price, rental rate, lead time or order book, even without a figure (\"rental rates for used trucks have been climbing this quarter\"); a general statement that demand stays strong or a product stays popular is not one;\n- a product, game, driver or benchmark specification with no business scale (\"the vacuum runs 60 minutes on a charge\"; \"a benchmark score\"), a retail price detail (\"a retailer marks one model down by $50\"), and a comparison the company, a partner or a third party publishes (\"the maker says its drug works twice as fast as older ones\"; \"a reviewer's test\"); it does not cover a competitor's comparison against the company's product, a partner's or customer's adoption or integration (also when a comparison shares its sentence), a reported launch, shipment, delay or cancellation of any of the company's products or a change to a product plan or configuration, including a reported sign that a planned product is going ahead (\"the long-range version of the jet is likely delayed or limited to a few deliveries\"; \"a parts supplier's catalogue lists the unannounced model\"), nor the company's decision to change the price it charges; uncertainty or a smaller product line does not make it a specification;\n- an unargued view or a quote that only characterises (\"the stock is a hold\"; \"a pivotal moment\"; \"an industry-leading platform\"), and a named analyst's reading of an event already recorded that adds no new fact or calculation (\"the recall shows quality risks are rising\"); it does not cover a reading that adds a new fact or calculation, nor the company's own statement that its plan, schedule or guidance still stands (\"the carmaker said the launch date has not moved\"), which is judged as the plan itself would be; a target price or valuation of the company is not kept, even with its assumptions and derivation, while the estimates it rests on are judged on their own (an analysts' earnings forecast is kept);\n- a political or strategic stance with no figure and no decision (\"diversifying suppliers will not reduce dependence\"); it does not cover a policy or regulatory step, nor a decision still in force that the item reports;\n- a share-price move, an investor's position or trade, or the market value (\"shares fell 13% this month\"; \"he is short the stock\"); it does not cover the news behind the move;\n- another company's matter that touches none of the company's markets (its valuation, share price, governance or a deal outside them), or that sits next to the company only by sharing an article, an event or an ecosystem; you supply the connection as the analyst and the item need not state it: a customer's spending, orders or backlog bears on demand, a supplier's capacity, output, prices or revenue on supply and input costs, a rival's products, prices or share in the company's markets on competition (\"a large customer's order backlog doubled\"; \"the main supplier's quarterly revenue jumped on demand for the part\");\n- the same fact said again in other words within this item: one deal, hire, programme or reported measure told in several sentences, with its terms, figures and growth rates, is one evidence item; keep the fuller wording (\"a $2 billion order for 120 stores in 15 countries over three years\"; \"cloud revenue of $8 billion, up 30% on the year and 6% on the quarter, 40% of the total\"); a deal one party signs under a wider programme, with its own amount or capacity, is its own evidence item, and a fact another outlet reported before is not a repeat within this item;\n- company boilerplate, bylines, forward-looking-statement text.\nA report and another party's denial or confirmation of it are two items, each kept only if it passes the test above; an estimate stays apart from any valuation drawn from it, and the valuation is not kept; one party's statement keeps its own planned or rumoured details.\nReturn only the evidence items you keep.\nThen check the theses and links. A new thesis that asks the same underlying question, about the same subject and scope, as an open thesis or another new thesis is not proposed: link its evidence to that thesis. A new thesis needs at least one kept evidence item, and a vague or noisy topic with no outcome to watch is not proposed. Each kept evidence item links to every thesis it informs and to no thesis its own relevance says it does not inform.\nFor each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the four reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it without links.\nAn item whose only home would be a new thesis that is not a big matter is returned with empty links and kept without links; an item an open thesis covers is linked there, not left without links. Then read back each statement you return with empty links that states the company's own figures: return it only if a figure can change what an analyst expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position; for example, a cash-rich company's balance or cash flow that the item ties to nothing usually cannot; return only what passes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c19-schema.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n \"type\": \"object\",\n \"additionalProperties\": false,\n \"required\": [\n  \"new_theses\",\n  \"evidence\"\n ],\n \"properties\": {\n  \"new_theses\": {\n   \"type\": \"array\",\n   \"description\": \"New thesis proposals, each referenced by at least one evidence link.\",\n   \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"required\": [\n     \"local_id\",\n     \"description\",\n     \"outcome\",\n     \"period\",\n     \"settles_on\",\n     \"outcomes\",\n     \"opens_as\",\n     \"settled_by\",\n     \"closest_open_thesis\",\n     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\n    ],\n    \"properties\": {\n     \"local_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Local reference for this new thesis in the answer; not a database ID.\"\n     },\n     \"description\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The proposed research question, stated clearly.\"\n     },\n     \"outcome\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The outcome or event being tracked by this thesis.\"\n     },\n     \"period\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The period or check date that settles the thesis: the one the item supports, or the one its reason fixes (section 3), with how it was set.\"\n     },\n     \"settles_on\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"pattern\": \"\\\\S\",\n      \"description\": \"The one figure for one period (a fiscal or calendar year, or a stated date), or the one event with its check date, whose result on that date settles this thesis. A thesis is a question, a fixed set of outcomes and a due date, written once: if no date and public material can place the answer in fixed outcomes (for example a figure over a rolling twelve months with no publication day, or several figures none of which leads), rewrite the thesis or do not propose it, and its statements are evidence.\"\n     },\n     \"outcomes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 2,\n      \"maxItems\": 5,\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\",\n       \"pattern\": \"\\\\S\"\n      },\n      \"description\": \"This thesis's fixed outcomes, written now: five ranges of that one figure, or the states of that one event (two for a yes/no, such as whether an unsigned deal is signed); checkable, not overlapping and leaving no gap, so that exactly one holds on the date; a middle range says what it is compared with. A company thesis's outcomes describe the business result; a shared quantity's or policy's describe only the result, not whether it is good.\"\n     },\n     \"opens_as\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n       \"product_node\",\n       \"binding_obligation\",\n       \"shared_quantity\",\n       \"policy_stage\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The reason this thesis opens, one of the four in section 3.\"\n     },\n     \"settled_by\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The public material that will settle the answer on a date (a filing, an official decision, a shipment confirmation, a statistics release).\",\n      \"pattern\": \"\\\\S\"\n     },\n     \"closest_open_thesis\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Exact ID of the open thesis closest to this one; null when the open list is empty.\"\n     },\n     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Why an analyst would bet on this question separately from the closest open thesis: how their answers can move apart.\"\n     }\n    }\n   }\n  },\n  \"evidence\": {\n   \"type\": \"array\",\n   \"description\": \"Evidence statements extracted from this item, with their thesis links.\",\n   \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"required\": [\n     \"local_id\",\n     \"summary\",\n     \"source_passages\",\n     \"original_party\",\n     \"reporting_speaker\",\n     \"tier\",\n     \"statement_date\",\n     \"statement_date_text\",\n     \"evidence_period\",\n     \"links\",\n     \"figures\"\n    ],\n    \"properties\": {\n     \"local_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Local reference for this evidence in the answer; not a database ID.\"\n     },\n     \"summary\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Standalone faithful summary naming the actor and preserving relevant figures, periods and conditions.\"\n     },\n     \"source_passages\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"description\": \"Contiguous verbatim passages from this source item that jointly support the summary; return each passage separately.\",\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n     },\n     \"original_party\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Party whose action, figure or claim is reported; null if unknown. Use the reporting outlet or author as the original party only for its own estimate, analysis or unnamed-source report.\"\n     },\n     \"reporting_speaker\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Person or outlet making or reporting the statement in this item, when known; null if unknown.\"\n     },\n     \"statement_date\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"pattern\": \"^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Original statement day as YYYY-MM-DD when known; null if the full day is unknown.\"\n     },\n     \"figures\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"object\",\n       \"additionalProperties\": false,\n       \"required\": [\n        \"measure\",\n        \"period\",\n        \"value\",\n        \"kind\",\n        \"basis\"\n       ],\n       \"properties\": {\n        \"measure\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"The financial measure as the passage states it.\"\n        },\n        \"period\": {\n         \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n           \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n           \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"The period as stated; null when none is given.\"\n        },\n        \"value\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"The figure copied exactly from one of this item's passages, with its unit.\"\n        },\n        \"kind\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"enum\": [\n          \"actual\",\n          \"guidance\",\n          \"estimate\"\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"actual: reported, including a balance as of a date; guidance: the company's own outlook; estimate: a named party's or consensus forecast.\"\n        },\n        \"basis\": {\n         \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n           \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n           \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"Scope and qualifications as stated (GAAP or non-GAAP, segment or company, conditions); null when none.\"\n        }\n       }\n      },\n      \"description\": \"The company's own useful financial figures this statement states (section 2, CONDITION); empty for any other statement. A statement with several useful figures stays one item and lists them all.\"\n     },\n     \"links\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 0,\n      \"description\": \"The existing or proposed theses this evidence informs; empty when it is material but no thesis takes it yet: it is kept in the company's record and linked when a covering thesis opens.\",\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"object\",\n       \"additionalProperties\": false,\n       \"required\": [\n        \"target_type\",\n        \"target_id\",\n        \"relevance\"\n       ],\n       \"properties\": {\n        \"target_type\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"enum\": [\n          \"existing\",\n          \"new\"\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"Whether the reference identifies an open thesis or a new proposal.\"\n        },\n        \"target_id\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"Exact supplied ID when existing, or local_id of a new thesis in this answer.\"\n        },\n        \"relevance\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"How this evidence informs the referenced thesis, distinguishing source claims from inference.\"\n        }\n       }\n      }\n     },\n     \"tier\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n       \"fact\",\n       \"party_statement\",\n       \"third_party_view\",\n       \"rumour\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Source tier of the statement; an unconfirmed or unnamed-source claim takes precedence as rumour.\"\n     },\n     \"statement_date_text\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Original date or partial date as stated in the item; null when absent.\"\n     },\n     \"evidence_period\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Period the fact, plan or forecast describes, as supported by the item; null when unknown.\"\n     }\n    }\n   }\n  }\n }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D417|unfiled|c19-schema|c8-schema' /Users/lchingen/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '272,320p' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"<p>开题理由是 D184 定的四类，D236 把主驱动量扩到产品节点，所以写成五类。判两件事，互不顶替：这是谁的问题（标的还是主题）；为什么值得开（开题理由）。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>类</th><th>开题理由</th><th>标的或主题</th><th>问什么</th><th>量还是事件</th><th>期间和到期</th><th>核对材料 <code>settled_by</code></th><th>出处</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>A</b> 主驱动量</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引：撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率、资本开支；跨行业如银行的净利息收入、零售商的同店销售、公用事业的费率基数、航空公司的燃油成本（当它是争论焦点时）。不是每一行报表数</td><td>量，五档</td><td>公司财年的今年或明年；到期日是这个数的发布日</td><td>公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报</td><td>D184：<code>settled_by</code> 是 \"the public material that resolves it\"；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>B</b> 主产品节点</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那一代产品哪天走到能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；发布、送样是它的证据，只有会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span></td><td>事件，五档，或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 1 条</span></td><td>能判出结果的那天</td><td>公司公告、发货确认</td><td>D236</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>C</b> 约束性义务</td><td><code>binding_obligation</code></td><td>标的</td><td>公司以自己名义承担的：为别人的债务、租约或收入担保或提供信用支持；借钱给别人；承诺购买（向别人买产能或服务也算）；为客户的产能或收入兜底；或写明规模、尚未完成的入股或收购<span class=\"src\">D236；收购按 D243 第 7 条</span>。规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开；够不上的单笔入股、收购、租约、授信不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条</span>。不算：自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。D239 选定的 role-v29 原文：\"Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations\"；D238 的记录写作 \"the company's own borrowing and leases and a completed or unsized stake do not\"</td><td>还没签：是非两档。已经承担（一笔或一个计划）：金额，五档</td><td>检查日最多在文章后 18 个月<span class=\"src\">D185</span>；已承担的按下一份年报</td><td>签约公告、年报承诺附注</td><td>D184、D185、D210、D236、D238、D243</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>D</b> 共同量</td><td><code>shared_quantity</code><span class=\"src\">D191、D243 第 2 条</span>；现行提示词和代码还叫 <code>industry_aggregate</code>，按这一页改</td><td>主题</td><td>任何一家公司之外、好几家都会受它影响的量或价格：几家公司的合计（云厂商资本开支）、价格（内存合约价、油价）、利率。同一总量的另一种人群、另一种说法是这个量的证据</td><td>量，五档</td><td>自然年的今年或明年。同一个量、同一年只有一个问题，由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>；量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算</td><td>几家公司年报、统计发布、官方决定</td><td>D184、D191、D197、D243；PRD 06</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>E</b> 政策阶段</td><td><code>policy_stage</code></td><td>问的是一家公司的收入、利润、份额或产品进度，算标的，即使由政策驱动；问的是世界上的事（许可制度、利率、合计支出），算主题。D184 采纳的 role-v12 原文：\"A question about a company's revenue, profit, share or product progress is an asset thesis; put its ticker in object, even when policy or macroeconomics drives it\"</td><td>一个政策或监管过程到了哪一步，写明谁说了算</td><td>事件，五档或两档</td><td>能判出那一步的那天。文章没写日期的待决监管事项，用本财年末（role-v12 原文：\"A pending regulatory decision may lack a date; use the current fiscal year-end as its due date\"）；这个日期是研究员定的检查日，要标明<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1 条</span></td><td>官方决定、公报</td><td>D184</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n<p>例子（跨行业）：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>A：</b>NVIDIA FY2027 数据中心收入；一家地区银行 FY2026 净利息收入；一家公用事业公司 2027 年费率基数。</li>\n<li><b>B：</b>下一代机架系统能否在 2027 年底前开始出货；一家车企的新平台能否在 2026 年内开始交付。</li>\n<li><b>C：</b>NVIDIA 为云客户产能兜底的义务在 FY2027 年报达到多少；一家保险公司是否在 2027 年中前为合资公司 5 亿美元债务签署担保。</li>\n<li><b>D：</b>五家最大云厂商 2026 年合计资本开支；2027 年 DRAM 合约价相对 2026 年的变化、美联储 2026 年最后一次会议后的利率上限。</li>\n<li><b>E：</b>中国是否在 2027-01-31 前正式批准本国公司进口 H200；美国是否在某日前对某类芯片实行出口许可。这两题问的是许可这件世界上的事，所以是主题，role-v12 原文的例子就是 \"licensing\"。一个监管决定对一家公司收入或产品进度的影响，问成那家公司的量或产品节点时，是标的问题（同一句原文）。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>五类之外的东西去哪</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>七类驱动不是问题类型。</b>它们是一条陈述为什么重要的理由，用来判分量和归档。D208 设计的\"每家公司种下的驱动问题\"由分析员开始覆盖时写好，不从文章里开；还没建。</li>\n<li><b>别家公司自己的量</b>（对手的份额、客户的资本开支）：D187 定了\"任何公司自己的量是那家公司的问题，私营公司也算\"，但还没实现，要先在覆盖名单里加私营公司这一类。D155 定了\"公司清单可以作为初始参考，但清单外不能忽略\"。现行代码在匹配时跳过名单外的对象<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Step 4</span>。所以抽取照常可以提这样的问题，它要过第 4 节的测试；名单外的现在会被匹配跳过，这不算抽取错。</li>\n<li><b>宏观量</b>（利率、通胀）：按 D 类共同量开题<span class=\"src\">D243 第 2 条</span>。只来自一篇纯宏观文章时，只有主题在名单上才开<span class=\"src\">D191 第 3 条</span>。宏观对每家公司的正负，在判断那家公司时读主题块决定<span class=\"src\">D191 第 1 条、D195</span>。</li>\n<li><b>开题理由是封闭的</b><span class=\"src\">D184</span>：一件事属不属于五类之一，按上表逐条看，比如一个监管决定看它是不是 E 类。哪一类都不属于的不开；它是不是证据、挂到哪，照第 5 节和归档规则。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>问题怎么写：PRD 06 的梯子规则，不重写</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>一个问题只问一个量的一个期间，或一件事；能各自朝相反方向走、而且分析员会分别下注的部分要分开<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 3 条；\"分别下注\"是 D248 加的，PRD 06 签字后更新</span>，分开的每一题都要过第 4 节的测试。</li>\n<li>写成问句，不写成断言<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Rationale</span>。</li>\n<li>结果档可核对、不重叠、不留缝，到期恰好一档成立；中间一档写明和什么比；\"小幅\"\"部分\"这种不能核对的说法不用，部分状态写成单独一档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 2 条</span>。标的问题的档描述业务结果；主题问题的档只写结局，不写好坏<span class=\"src\">PRD 06、D186</span>。</li>\n<li>到期日：量是它的发布日；事件是能判出结果的那天。公司的量用公司财年，别的用自然年，只开今年和明年<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；约束性义务例外，D185</span>。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 id=\"opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</h2>\n<blockquote><p><b>一个问题值得单独追，要同时满足三件事：它的答案可能改变仓位；能在一个日期用公开材料判出落在哪一档；库里没有问题在问同一件事。</b>开多少个是判断的结果，不是目标<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6；评审 §1</span>。</p>\n<p>颗粒度按一个高端对冲基金分析员：只有会单独下注的大事开题，鸡毛蒜皮不开题（它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判）；同一个赌注的几种说法是一题，截止日、里程碑、财年和日历年各按本节\"同一题、续期，还是另一题\"里的那一条判<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</p>\n<p>另有一条前提：新问题要有独立的投资判断；一个新产品、一个新数字、一个更窄的范围，单凭这些不开<span class=\"src\">D201</span>。</p></blockquote>\n\n<h3>四个测试<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6</span></h3>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><b>值得追</b>写得出\"这个结果会改变哪项收入、利润、现金或信用风险、竞争位置\"吗？写不出就留作证据，不开题。\"数字很大\"不算理由。单笔交易、产品、项目，规模够不上改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险的，不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条：问的就是小交易、小产品</span>；这一测试的其余理由（包括竞争位置）不变。</li>\n<li><b>独立意义</b>能写出两个情景吗：其他问题的答案不变，只有这一题相反，而对业务的判断确实不同？写不出就优先作为证据<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 3、8 条</span>。评审里的一个判例：NVIDIA FY2027 总收入题判为数据中心收入题的证据，理由是\"该段明确说主要增长来自数据中心，未提出独立的其他业务争论\"。这是对那一段材料的判断，别的材料要逐个判。</li>\n<li><b>能核对</b>有一个日期和一份公开材料能把答案放进事先固定的档吗？没有就重写问题。到期没有材料记\"未能判定\"，不算错。</li>\n<li><b>不是重复</b>和已有问题比，只是预测值、措辞、来源、方向或同一总量的另一种口径不同，最终核对的是同一个结果吗？是就是同一题。抽取看不到库<span class=\"src\">D211</span>，这一条在抽取时只对同一篇文章里提出的几个问题判；和库里的比由匹配做。</li>\n</ol>\n<p>另外三条写法检查<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1、5、6 条</span>。没过的问题不能照原样开，要重写；重写不了就不开，材料作证据。</p>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 35 -B 3 '\"'^## D417|''^### D417|D417[ :：.]'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"4603-- **Evidence behind the question:** `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/result-3/RESULT.md`, `wait-as-ruling-out-hand-read.md`, `wait-accounts.json`.\n4604-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step. It amends the shape D409 gave an event's answer, if it passes.\n4605-\n4606:## D417 · 2026-11-10 · A figure for a rolling twelve months with no publication day in the texts is declined\n4607-\n4608-- **Asked:** \"有两道题问的是“某项调查统计的未来 12 个月里，中国企业把多少 AI 芯片预算给国产”。这不是整年数字，文章也没说后续调查哪天公布。到期日改由程序定之后，系统对这两道题基本不出题了（6 次里 5 次），理由是“没有能核对的公布日期”。这是新出现的行为，你还没确认过；两位裁决读者对它也意见相反，第 4 条线过不过就取决于它。怎么定？\"\n4609-  - Options: confirm, no judged question (recommended): \"滚动 12 个月、又没有公布日期的数字，不写成判断题，如实说明理由。代价：这两道题不再有可判的问题。\"; write the question with the period's last day as its due day (the follow-up survey may not exist that day; a further rule to build and prove).\n4610-  - Alex: \"确认：这类题不出题 (Recommended)\".\n4611-- **Decided:** a figure that covers a period which is not one fiscal or calendar year (a survey's rolling twelve months) and\n4612-  for which neither the topic nor the item gives a publication day is declined, with that reason. The cost he was shown: such\n4613-  topics get no judged question. This confirms the behaviour D414's refusal produced and that was reported as not confirmed.\n4614-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step; mark N of the readers' form.\n4615-\n4616-## D418 · 2026-11-10 · A government's permission or ban on a class of product belongs to the theme, not to the company\n4617-\n4618-- **Asked:** \"“中国政府是否放行英伟达 H200 芯片在华销售”这类题，系统大多归在“英伟达”名下，有时归在行业主题“芯片出口管制”名下，同一道题三次归属还会不一致。第三次测试里归在公司名下的 5 份，两类读者都判为归错了，认为应归行业主题。区别是：归行业主题的题会给每家相关公司的判断都看到，归公司的只给这一家看。归哪边？\"\n4619-  - Options: the theme \"chip-export-controls\" (recommended): \"两类读者意见一致。我需要在提示词里加一条归属规则（政府对某类产品的放行或禁令归行业主题），并先小额验证不带坏别的题，比如法国对英伟达本身的反垄断调查仍归公司。\"; the company (the readers' form would then be changed to that reading).\n4620-  - Alex: \"归行业主题“芯片出口管制” (Recommended)\".\n4621-- **Decided:** a question about a government's or regulator's permission, restriction or ban on a class of products or trade\n4622-  belongs to the theme that covers it, also when the product is the company's own. A proceeding against the company itself (an\n4623-  investigation of its conduct, a fine) stays the company's. A rule in the request, proved small before any measurement, with\n4624-  the French investigation as the case that must not move.\n4625-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step; mark O of the readers' form.\n4626-\n4627-## D419 · 2026-11-10 · The fourth Stage A is sent without asking again once each change is proved small and reviewed\n4628-\n4629-- **Asked:** \"上面你选的改动，各自小额验证通过并过评审之后，第四次正式测试（同样 44 道题各三次，约 0.11 美元；目前累计约 0.76 美元，上限 3 美元）怎么发？再测一次也不能保证一份错都没有，读者松紧不一的问题也还在。\"\n4630-  - Options: send once the checks pass (recommended): \"和上次一样：每项改动先单独小额验证并过评审，任何一项没通过就停下来找你，不发正式测试。\"; ask again before the send.\n4631-  - Alex: \"验证通过就直接发 (Recommended)\".\n4632:- **Decided:** as D415, for the changes of D416, D417 and D418: each is proved small and reviewed in the council; when all pass\n4633-  the fourth Stage A (the same 44 theses, three sends each, within D401's $3) is sent without asking again; a change that does\n4634-  not pass stops the line and goes to him. He was told that a further run cannot be promised to have no fault and that the\n4635-  reader families still part. Stage B still needs his word.\n4636-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step.\n4637-\n4638-## D420 · 2026-11-10 · A proceeding that formally ends without the conclusion the question asks for is ruled out; the question stays\n4639-\n4640-- **Asked:** \"题目问的是“法国竞争管理局会不会在 2027 年 1 月 31 日前公布对英伟达反垄断调查的结论”。到期前可能有三种情况：① 公布结案决定（哪怕不处罚），算“发生了”；③ 调查还在继续，算“还在等”。这两点没有争议。有争议的是 ②：当局正式宣布放弃或撤回调查，但没有公布题目问的那种结论。模型每次写法不一样，读者也各执一词。② 算什么？\"\n4641-  - Options: it is ruled out (recommended): \"题目保持原样，问的仍是“有没有公布结论”。这类题固定有三种结果：公布了／当局正式放弃且没有结论／还在查。这也是目前多数已存答案的写法，且符合现有规则“判题目点名追踪的那件事”。不写“明确落空”的答案将算错。\"; ask instead whether the investigation is over (two outcomes; it tracks another event than the conclusion the thesis names).\n4642-  - Alex: \"② 算“明确落空” (Recommended)\".\n4643-- **Decided:** for a proceeding an authority conducts and whose asked-for event is its published decision or conclusion: a\n4644-  published closing decision, with or without a penalty, is the event happened; the authority formally abandoning or\n4645-  withdrawing the proceeding without that decision or conclusion is the event ruled out; the proceeding still going on the due\n4646-  day is the wait. Such an event always has a ruling out, and an answer that names none, or that writes the authority's\n4647-  decision to go on as the ruling out, is at fault. The judged question stays the one the thesis's outcome names.\n4648-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step; mark R of the readers' form.\n4649-\n4650-## D421 · 2026-11-10 · Each further change is tested alone; all passing, the fourth Stage A is sent without asking again\n4651-\n4652-- **Asked:** \"接下来怎么走？我建议每项改动单独测，不再捆在一起：(a) 把你上一题的定义写进提示词，在三道法国调查题上单独测；(b) 把归属规则收窄成“题目追踪的是政府决定本身才归行业主题，追踪公司自己销售的仍归公司”，单独测；(c) 在 (a) 之后把“分两格填”再单独测一次，停止条件不变。调查题不出题那条直接并入。三项合计约 10 美分；第四次正式测试约 11 美分；目前累计 0.90 美元，上限 3 美元。\"\n4653-  - Options: test the three apart and send the fourth Stage A when all pass (recommended): \"(a)(b)(c) 各自小额验证并过评审。全部通过就直接发第四次正式测试；任何一项没通过就停下来找你。\"; drop the typed shape and do (a) and (b) only; test the three and ask before the fourth Stage A; stop here.\n4654-  - Alex: \"三项分别测，全过就直接发第四次 (Recommended)\".\n4655:- **Decided:** D417 goes into the working request. Then, each beside the working request and on its own: (a) D420's rule in the\n4656-  request, on the three French theses; (b) D418's sentence narrowed (the theme when the tracked outcome is the government's\n4657-  decision; the company when it is the company's own sales under it); (c) after (a), the typed ruling out once more, the same\n4658-  stop condition as before. Each is reviewed in the council. When all three pass, the fourth Stage A (the same 44 theses,\n4659-  three sends each, within D401's $3) is sent without asking again; one that does not pass stops the line and goes to him.\n4660-  Stage B still needs his word. This replaces D419's terms for these changes.\n4661-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step.\n4662-\n4663-## D422 · 2026-11-10 · A second look by the model at its own answer is tested small, as a candidate; adoption is Alex's after the result\n4664-\n4665-- **Asked:** \"第四次正式测试仍有 3 条线各差 1 到 3 份。剩下的错都是同一种：模型懂规则，一遍写下来偶尔滑过去，事后问它它能自己指出来。我的建议是先做一个小额测试：让模型对自己的答案“再看一遍”（多发一次请求，只说“请对照规则逐条检查，没错就原样返回，有错就改正”，不提示哪里有错）。用第四次测试的 66 份已存答案（18 份读者公认有错、18 份有争议、30 份没人挑出错），约 7 美分。这和你定过的“复核要写在同一个提示词末尾”不一样，所以必须由你定。下一步怎么走？\"\n4666-  - Options: the small test of a second look (recommended): \"只是候选做法，不是已证明的修法。通过条件事先写死：18 份公认有错的至少改好 9 份，且 30 份没错的最多改坏 1 份；第二遍的答案若过不了程序检查就沿用第一遍。改过的答案由两类读者盲读。通过也只说明“值得带着它再正式测一次”，不等于六条线过了。若采用，每道新题多一次请求，约多花 0.1 美分和 10 到 20 秒。做完我把结果报给你，再由你定是否采用。\"; go on class by class (the unjustified declines first); open Stage B on the step as it stands (his to waive his lines); stop.\n4667-  - Alex: \"先做“再看一遍”的小额测试 (Recommended)\".\n4668-- **Decided:** the test designed in `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/probe-second-look-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` is run: 66 stored\n4669-  answers of the fourth Stage A (18 with a fault the readers agree on, 18 with a disputed one only, 30 that no reader\n4670-  faults), each sent back once with one instruction that names no fault; the changed answers read blind by the two reader\n4671-  families; passing means at least 9 of the 18 mended and at most 1 of the 30 damaged. A second answer that code refuses\n4672-  leaves the first in place. The result goes to him, and whether the step takes a second look is decided by him then: this\n4673-  decision opens the test and nothing more. It is a departure, for this test, from AGENTS §6's check at the end of the same\n4674-  prompt, which stays in the request.\n4675-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step.\n4676-\n4677-## D423 · 2026-11-10 · Work on Jev's revision relation stops; \"a later version does not take the older record's questions\" is accepted as a direction and, once measured, withdrawn by its author; the rule stays, pending Alex\n4678-\n4679-- **Asked** (after the traced case of the Step 2 log §15): \"建议停止在 Jev 的“更新关系”上投入。它作为已知缺陷留在清单上 … Step 2 和 Jev 都不改。\" and\n4680-  \"有一件事等你定，不急。… B 被判为 A 的更新版后，要不要让 B 自动挂到 A 的所有问题下面？ 不自动挂（我的建议）：这次带进去的 5 条里，2 条错、1 条说不清、\n4681-  2 条有用。 保持自动挂。\"\n4682-  - Alex: \"okay take your suggestion what is the fix and how to measure get your council skill ready to propose\".\n4683-- **Decided by those words:** no further work on Jev's revision relation now; the defect stays open with its counts. The direction\n4684-  \"not automatically\" is accepted, and the council loop is to propose the fix and its measurement before anything is built.\n4685-- **What the council round found** (`clean-arch/step2-revision-links-2026-11-10/LOG.md`): on the three saved draws the rule wrote 24\n4686-  links (5 of 700, 11 of 725, 8 of 730). Two blind reader families: 19 context by both, 3 evidence by both, 2 split. Nothing a\n4687-  program can read separates the two kinds. One context link judged both ways: rung 2 in six of six. One evidence link judged both\n4688-  ways (NVIDIA's answer beside four reports under FY2028 revenue): rung 2, 2, 2 with it and 2, 3, 2 without, not decided by the rule\n4689-  fixed beforehand. The suggestion rested on draw 1 alone and is withdrawn by its author; Codex agrees that the rule is not changed\n4690-  now and does not agree that the present rule is shown to be better.\n--\n5172-  controlled change could show.\n5173-- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-codex-9.md`): \"Write and independently review the status report first; then\n5174-  continue to the $0 identity-design comparison, with F6 recorded as a contradiction whose standalone impact remains uncertain.\"\n5175:- **Decided:** F6 is not tested on its own; its correction, with the date safeguards of round 8 (no invented release day; D417 intact), waits\n5176-  for the next clean Step 1 version and is not bundled silently. Next, a status report for Alex (goal, results under both treatments,\n5177-  what traces can and cannot establish, Stage A failed, Stage B's full-run reading largely unmeasured, D427 outstanding, production's\n5178-  unlinked facts not a shown loss, opening opportunities not right answers), reviewed by the council for accuracy; then the $0 comparison of\n5179-  a general prompt change against a matching-stage design for the identity boundaries.\n5180-\n5181-## D463 · 2026-11-13 · The identity lever: a general prompt clause first (P), written and probe-designed before any send (council consensus under D439)\n5182-\n5183-- **Comparison** (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/step1-audit/IDENTITY-COMPARISON.md`): production, which also sees the open\n5184-  questions, says \"a different population, source, estimate, wording or direction of a question is the same question; a different\n5185-  quantity, period or decision is another\" and opens both capex years in 5 of 6 draws and the Ohio signing in 4 of 6 (clean c8: 1 and 1);\n5186-  production never opens a memory question (0 of 6), and the stopped c14/c15yc year sentence moved c8's memory question (D441). A matching\n5187-  stage cannot recover a question Step 1 never proposes unless Step 1 stops judging identity (a larger architectural change).\n5188-- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-codex-12.md`): production is a lead, not a controlled proof (its workflow\n5189-  proposes candidates that may already be open and code compares them afterward); P can repeat the memory regression; \"a different\n5190-  quantity, period or decision is another\" is too broad alone (a later deadline of one event is evidence while the earlier is open; a\n5191-  comparison names two periods and asks one); the unsigned-deal case permits a separate question when independently worthwhile; two or\n5192-  three general examples per class; a frozen fresh-article probe with reader-marked expectations, denominators, minimum effects, an\n5193-  inconclusive outcome and exercised positive controls. \"Proceed to a general written P candidate and a reviewed fresh-article probe design\n5194-  with these corrections; do not send until the cases, controls, thresholds and regression handling are concrete and the council has\n5195-  reviewed them.\"\n5196-- **Decided:** write the candidate (c16, from c8, the identity clause only; F6 not included) and the probe design (fresh articles after\n5197-  2026-07-14 never sent in a Step 1 measurement, frozen before any answer is read, an independent reader's expected behaviour per article,\n5198-  a full-run draw's library at 2026-07-14 as a controlled snapshot, the stopped capex, Ohio and memory articles as guards), both reviewed by\n5199-  the council before any send.\n5200-\n5201-## D464 · 2026-11-13 · Send the case-specific identity diagnostic, c16 version 5 against c8, under one $5 ledger (council consensus under D439)\n5202-\n5203-- **Rounds** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-codex-13.md`–`mt-codex-15.md`): the candidate went through four blind audits\n5204-  (versions 1, 3, 4 read by fresh Codex readers; version 5 answers the last, wording-level points); the selection was redone with four\n5205-  blind category readers over 80 candidates and twenty more for T1 and T3, which showed that this window holds **one fresh story per target\n5206-  boundary** (next year's hyperscaler capex; the OpenAI Ohio guarantee) and no independent positive comparison story; the design became a\n5207-  case-specific diagnostic: targets reported per story, regression lines on 7 merge stories, 9 negative stories and the stored guards\n5208-  (memory with nine sends a state and a stop on D441's shape, capex-repeat-a, population), validity minima, article-to-story counting, one\n5209-  invocation and one ledger. Round 15's two blocks were fixed and proved at $0: a memory validity minimum (7 valid sends a state) and the\n5210-  ledger settling missing, malformed or zero-priced usage at its reservation (`identity-probe/probe_identity.py`, five tests, a mutant\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"**The two new fields introduce several ways to lose or narrow a valid research question.** The biggest risk is treating “one figure” as one raw number, which can turn “next year compared with this year” into “next year’s number” and lose the comparison the analyst wanted to track.\n\nI ran the requested diffs. The system texts are identical, as are the closing checks. The schema diff adds the two required fields and their definitions; the only other difference is the final newline.\n\n### Sentence-by-sentence audit\n\n| New description | Verdict | Signed standard and assessment |\n|---|---|---|\n| **`settles_on`, sentence 1:** “The one figure for one period … or the one event with its check date, whose result on that date settles this thesis.” | **Keeps narrower** | §3 says: “一个问题只问一个量的一个期间，或一件事” and gives “2027 年 DRAM 合约价相对 2026 年的变化” as an example. A change from one year to another is one tracked quantity, but “the one figure for one period” can be read as requiring one year’s raw figure. It also blurs the distinction in §3: “量是它的发布日；事件是能判出结果的那天.” A stated date for a figure is not necessarily its period or publication date. |\n| **`settles_on`, sentence 2:** “A thesis is a question, a fixed set of outcomes and a due date, written once: if no date and public material can place the answer in fixed outcomes … rewrite the thesis or do not propose it, and its statements are evidence.” | **Contradicts**, in part | The first clause matches the standard’s “一个问题句、一组结果档、一个到期日，写下后不改.” §4 says: “有一个日期和一份公开材料能把答案放进事先固定的档吗？没有就重写问题.” But the unconditional “its statements are evidence” conflicts with §4’s “它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判.” Also, “several figures none of which leads” has **no source** as an automatic reason to rewrite or reject: §3 instead separates parts only when they can move apart **and** an analyst would bet on them separately. |\n| **`outcomes`, sentence 1:** “This thesis’s fixed outcomes, written now: five ranges of that one figure, or the states of that one event …; checkable, not overlapping and leaving no gap …” | **Keeps narrower** | The checks themselves match §3: “结果档可核对、不重叠、不留缝，到期恰好一档成立；中间一档写明和什么比.” The table supports five ranges for a quantity and two for an unsigned obligation. But “five ranges of that one figure” repeats the risk that a valid **change between two years** is reduced to one raw figure. For events, §3 permits “五档，或是非两档”; the description does not explicitly preserve the five-state option, although its wording does not prohibit it. |\n| **`outcomes`, sentence 2:** “A company thesis’s outcomes describe the business result; a shared quantity’s or policy’s describe only the result, not whether it is good.” | **Contradicts**, for policy | §3 says: “标的问题的档描述业务结果；主题问题的档只写结局，不写好坏.” A policy-driven question is not automatically a theme: the policy row says a question about “一家公司的收入、利润、份额或产品进度，算标的，即使由政策驱动.” The new sentence assigns **all** policy questions the theme treatment, including company questions. |\n\nD417 supports the particular refusal of a **non-annual rolling period with no publication day supplied by the topic or item**. It does not establish a general ban on every question mentioning multiple figures. Its recorded scope is the clean path’s later judging step, so applying its example here should not silently widen that decision.\n\n### Conflicts inside the request\n\n- **When to open:** “several figures none of which leads” can cause rejection or rewriting solely because several figures appear. The system instead asks whether the answer can change the business and whether the analyst would bet on it separately. It does not say a multi-figure question fails merely because no figure “leads.”\n- **Dates:** “whose result on that date” can suggest that the result itself must occur or be published on the check date. The system gives different rules by reason: next annual report for an undertaken obligation, a check within 18 months for an unsigned one, fiscal year-end for an undated pending regulatory decision, and a supported release or check date for shared quantities and product events. The new wording does not restate those distinctions and can pull the model toward a stricter reading.\n- **Evidence without a thesis:** “its statements are evidence” can be read as keeping every statement after a thesis is rejected. The system and closing check require each statement to pass the evidence test independently. A passing statement can link to an existing thesis or remain unlinked.\n- **Separate bets:** Rewriting a complex question to satisfy “one figure” or “one event” can create a smaller question that no longer merits a separate bet, even though the original question did. The system explicitly says to open only matters an analyst would bet on separately.\n\nThese are conflicts or ambiguities in the wording; this read-only review does not establish how often a model would act on them.\n\n### Industry neutrality\n\nThe new descriptions use generic concepts and name **no covered company, product or specific numerical business figure**. “Unsigned deal” and a rolling twelve-month survey are general examples. However, the policy sentence does **not** apply the same distinction across all cases: it treats policy questions as theme questions even when the standard classifies a policy-driven business outcome as a company question.\n\n### Concrete risks to valid questions\n\n- **Next year versus this year:** “one figure for one period” and “five ranges of that one figure” could change “How much will next year’s contract price rise or fall versus this year?” into “What will next year’s price be?” The first tracks a change; the second can lose it. The standard explicitly gives a next-year-versus-current-year comparison.\n- **Unsigned deal:** The example “whether an unsigned deal is signed” supports a yes/no question. But **“whose result on that date”** could be misread as requiring the signing to occur on the check date, instead of asking whether it was signed **by** that date. The standard allows an unsigned obligation to be checked within 18 months.\n- **Product shipment:** The same phrase could turn “Will shipments begin by the date?” into “Will shipments begin on that date?” or discourage a proposal when the article supports a check date but not the exact day shipments will begin. The standard tracks the main product reaching the revenue-producing step and checks it when the outcome can be determined.\n- **Several related figures:** “several figures none of which leads” could discard or narrow a single economically meaningful question before asking whether its parts can move apart and justify separate bets. Conversely, if they do justify separate bets, the standard calls for separate questions, each passing the opening tests.\n\nSources: [signed extraction standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:272), [D417](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4606), and [candidate schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c19-schema.json:51)."}}
